From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:55:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: real GCC output as a test, scalar float memory
 intrinsics, a linker-message reader that handles French
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

test_aot_realistic.py compiles realistic_sample.c (own C) with aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc and compares the AOT
and AOT+JIT results with Unicorn: loops, memory, byte loads, 128-bit multiplies, float comparisons and
32/64-bit exclusive loops are identical. It pins what does not work yet: a jump table is an explicit error
in AOT-only and one JIT entry per dispatch with the JIT; six of twenty functions (vector and scalar FP
Remill cannot lift, byte and halfword exclusives) and the nine mnemonics behind them are listed.
The runtime gets __remill_read/write_memory_f32/f64 (found missing by compiled code). aot_lift.missing_symbols
reads the linker's complaint in English and French (the « name » of the French one has a space inside).

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: tests and fixes of the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); nothing in the host, loader or shader chain changes
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t4-jit-secours)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
